[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Improved Lodge Storage connects the Lodge's unlimited storage to its basement crafting stations and adds storage access at the New Atlantis Spaceport. It also adds buildable access points for Lodge Storage and ship cargo in homes, outposts, and aboard your ship. Building a Lodge Storage access point makes its resources available for crafting, research, and construction in the same home, outpost, or ship.

Every Lodge Storage access point opens the same unlimited inventory: the original safe in your Lodge bedroom. Every Ship Cargo access point opens your current home ship's cargo hold. Items remain in their original inventories.

[size=4][b]Craft directly from Lodge storage[/b][/size]
All six crafting and research stations in the Lodge basement can use resources from your Lodge storage, alongside your personal inventory and the game's normal access to ship cargo. Keep your materials in the safe and craft without carrying them around.

[size=4][b]Ship cargo in the basement[/b][/size]
A blue [b]Ship Cargo[/b] panel beside the basement locker opens your current home ship's cargo hold. Transfer supplies between your ship, your inventory, and Lodge storage without leaving the crafting area. The panel automatically follows your choice of home ship.

[size=4][b]Build storage access in homes, outposts, and ships[/b][/size]
Two wall-mounted devices are available under [b]Misc[/b] in the build menu for player homes and outposts, and in your ship's Decorate menu:
[list]
[*][b]Lodge Storage:[/b] a Captain's Locker that opens your shared Lodge inventory.[/*]
[*][b]Ship Cargo:[/b] a blue cargo panel that opens your current home ship's cargo hold.[/*]
[/list]
Both are free to build and require no research or perks. Removing an access point does not remove any stored items.

Building a [b]Lodge Storage[/b] access point also lets you craft, research, and build using Lodge resources in the same home, outpost, or ship.

If access to Lodge Storage at distant outposts breaks your immersion, simply don't build Lodge Storage access points there.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the downloaded archive with your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Enable [b]ImprovedLodgeStorage.esm[/b].[/*]
[*]Restart Starfield.[/*]
[/list]
For manual installation, extract the archive into Starfield's [b]Data[/b] folder and enable [b]ImprovedLodgeStorage.esm[/b] in your plugin list.

[size=4][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
When you open the build menu in a home, outpost, or ship with a Lodge Storage access point, items that require Lodge materials may initially appear unavailable. This is a visual glitch: the menu is displayed before the storage connection is established. You can still build those items. Switch to another tab and back to refresh the display.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Close any crafting, research, or build menus and save your game before disabling the mod. Then disable it in your mod manager and restart Starfield. Your items remain in the original Lodge bedroom safe and are still accessible there. The added containers are access points to existing inventories, so you do not need to empty them before uninstalling.

If you save your game while a temporary storage connection is active and then uninstall the mod, the affected home, outpost, or ship may retain access to Lodge Storage. Re-enabling the mod and loading the affected save may clear the connection. If access persists after closing the menus and disabling the mod again, manual cleanup or an earlier save is needed.

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Source code and build instructions: [url=https://github.com/kayahr/ImprovedLodgeStorage]https://github.com/kayahr/ImprovedLodgeStorage[/url]
